<title>USA: Wheelabrator sees charges from Wessex deal.</title>
<headline>Wheelabrator sees charges from Wessex deal.</headline>
<dateline>HAMPTON, N.H. 1996-12-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Wheelabrator Technologies Inc said Wednesday it expects to take a charge of about $20 million, or $0.12 a share, in the fourth quarter related to Waste Management International Plc's agreement to sell its stake in Wessex Water Plc.</p>
<p>Waste Management is 12 percent owned by Wheelaborator.</p>
<p>Wheelaborator said the Wessex deal is also expected to cut its 1997 earnings by about $0.03 a share.  </p>
<p>Earlier today Waste Management said it decided to sell its 19.5 percent equity investment in Wessex.</p>
<p>((-- Chicago Newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
</text>
